    "full_body": "## V11 owner checkpoint: complete baseline plus explicit current companion\n\nAll ten adoption gates remain OPEN. Scientific acceptance is HOLD, the adoption action is NoUpdate, and production adoption is false.\n\n### What changed\n\nThis update preserves the entire original 134,567-byte BLOCKERS.json at blob `2d5f0256776089b386f8e5ebd9d9eefcbfaac5f2` and adds OWNER_FOLLOWUP_V11.json with current publication identities and explicitly scoped new observations. Every original gate, intake, closure requirement and all eighteen previous completed-work entries remain byte-for-byte unchanged. Reading only BLOCKERS.json returns historical V10 execution context; both components together are this V11 checkpoint.\n\nThe companion binds the actual cead source publication in #5935 and the actual V17 evidence publication `21df04700aa885aef72b70962f270b966a112de6` in #5889, with their complete original publication receipts and PR/ref readbacks. Twelve original full reports are verified; six older selected local proof files remain unavailable and are not reconstructed.\n\nThe exact V11 source gate and clean Windows helper/scoped-fix qualification passed. Prior d0f MEM/Architecture/Private and two-case native results keep their exact source boundaries. Original d0f blocking is completed / failure, with 37 terminal jobs: 24 success / 4 failure / 5 cancelled / 4 skipped. All 28 recovered original job logs are byte-bound; original parser/profile gaps remain explicit.\n\n### Current CI and unresolved mechanisms\n\nThe earlier cead five-workflow snapshot at 19:02:55 UTC remains historical. A separate complete 19:08 packet retains ten original API bodies and the full 1,303,056-byte GNU failure log in five exact parts; every payload and complete file hash was independently checked. FLAKY remains distinct from strict pass, the displayed Rust block is not the whole case universe, and the current musl test-stage failure is separate from old d0f dependency cancellation. A later root observation at 19:10:49 UTC shows blocking still in progress, with Mac Intel, musl and GNU already failed at their original Bazel test steps. No current-head required-CI acceptance or transfer of earlier d0f passes is claimed.\n\nThe elevated outside-root delete boundary, memory coverage failure, timeout/flaky native scopes, original provider terminal/physical request count, original H V3/V4 effects and independent owner/trust/effect recovery remain open. V12 is only a reviewed diagnostic patch: no V12 source commit, source gate or native run exists.\n\n### Verification and review\n\nThe full baseline and every new file are verified at the candidate and actual published head. Validation consists of immutable Git full-file reads, exact byte/hash checks, original-report JSON pointer checks and independent static reviews. The managed local environment is unavailable, and the frozen Python owner generator was not run for this explicit companion.\n\n[Review entry point](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/blob/781f675fba693a0717e9326442547e2d86c1a7ef/qualification/memory-cell-mem8-owner/run-001/OWNER_CHECKPOINT_V11.md)\n[Complete unchanged baseline](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/blob/781f675fba693a0717e9326442547e2d86c1a7ef/qualification/memory-cell-mem8-owner/run-001/BLOCKERS.json)\n[Current companion](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/blob/781f675fba693a0717e9326442547e2d86c1a7ef/qualification/memory-cell-mem8-owner/run-001/OWNER_FOLLOWUP_V11.json)\n[Complete V17 evidence checkpoint](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/blob/21df04700aa885aef72b70962f270b966a112de6/qualification/memory-cell-mem8-ci-followup/CHECKPOINT_REPAIR_V17.md)\n\nOriginal owner base `943196eb18a1a04e7248307cf8708bed38b82b8b` is retained. This PR remains draft. No new real model generation, scored actor episode, unknown-request replay, H mutation, merge or deployment is claimed.\n"
  },
